# Real files win. Without these four lines the catch-all below swallows them,
# and a crawler asking for robots.txt is handed the website — which is what was
# happening.
/robots.txt    /robots.txt    200
/sitemap.xml   /sitemap.xml   200
/llms.txt      /llms.txt      200
/_headers      /_headers      200

# Every remaining address is the app. Pre-rendered documents sit at their own
# paths as real files and are served before this is consulted, so what a
# crawler gets is that page rather than the front one.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the address must stay what the reader typed, or the
# routing has nothing to read.
/*  /index.html  200
